1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,360
Breaking. Democrats are pushing to ban AI superintelligence, with up to 20 years in prison

2
00:00:05,360 --> 00:00:06,500
for violating the law.

3
00:00:06,700 --> 00:00:11,540
"- We have to ban, B-A-N, the development of superintelligence."

4
00:00:11,540 --> 00:00:18,620
"- You're also proposing a penalty, 20 years in prison for those who don't abide by those rules."

5
00:00:18,620 --> 00:00:19,580
"- Yeah, that's right."

6
00:00:19,580 --> 00:00:24,460
Arizona congresswoman Yasemin Ansari says stopping advanced AI development should be

7
00:00:24,460 --> 00:00:28,300
a day one priority for Democrats. And there's already a bill to make it happen.

8
00:00:28,300 --> 00:00:32,840
In September, Bernie Sanders and Greg Kassar introduced legislation that would permanently

9
00:00:32,840 --> 00:00:38,020
ban artificial superintelligence. But it doesn't stop there. The proposal would temporarily pause

10
00:00:38,020 --> 00:00:43,080
advanced AI development until a new federal regulator establishes safety rules. It would

11
00:00:43,080 --> 00:00:47,300
create an entire Department of Artificial Intelligence to monitor powerful AI models.

12
00:00:47,740 --> 00:00:51,700
And companies that violate the ban could face what lawmakers call the corporate death

13
00:00:51,700 --> 00:00:56,440
penalty. Individuals could face up to 20 years in federal prison. And this comes after

14
00:00:56,440 --> 00:01:01,180
an NBC exit poll found that 56 percent of voters considered AI and data centers

15
00:01:01,180 --> 00:01:04,180
a crucial or major factor in their midterm vote.

16
00:01:05,200 --> 00:01:09,940
Supporters say the restrictions would protect humanity from AI systems beyond human control.

17
00:01:10,360 --> 00:01:14,300
Critics warn sweeping restrictions could slow innovation and put America at a disadvantage.

18
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,560
The bill has not become law. So here's the question.

19
00:01:18,620 --> 00:01:22,020
Can Washington regulate superintelligence before it even exists?
